# Extracting Domain from URL String

Here are several ways to extract the domain from a URL string in different languages:

---

## Python

```python
from urllib.parse import urlparse

def extract_domain(url: str) -> str:
    """Extract the domain (hostname) from a URL string."""
    parsed = urlparse(url)
    return parsed.hostname or ''

# Examples
print(extract_domain("https://www.example.com/path/to/page"))        # www.example.com
print(extract_domain("http://example.org:8080"))                      # example.org
print(extract_domain("https://sub.domain.example.co.uk/page"))        # sub.domain.example.co.uk
```

### Extract Just the Base Domain (without subdomains)

```python
from tldextract import extract

def extract_base_domain(url: str) -> str:
    """Extract the registered domain (e.g., example.com from sub.example.com)."""
    parsed = urlparse(url)
    domain = parsed.hostname
    if domain:
        parts = extract(domain)
        return f"{parts.domain}.{parts.suffix}"
    return ''

print(extract_base_domain("https://www.sub.example.co.uk/page"))  # example.co.uk
```

