   public class Singleton {
       private Singleton() {}

       private static class SingletonHelper {
           private static final Singleton INSTANCE = new Singleton();
       }

       public static Singleton getInstance() {
           return SingletonHelper.INSTANCE;
       }
   }
   ```
   - Why it works: The inner static class is only loaded when `getInstance()` is called, ensuring lazy initialization. The JVM guarantees thread-safe class loading.

5.  **Draft - Enum Singleton (Also Highly Recommended):**
