### **C#**
In C#, you can use the `Count` property or the `Any()` method from LINQ.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

class Program {
    static void Main() {
        List<string> myList = new List<string>();

        if (myList.Count == 0) {
            Console.WriteLine("The list is empty.");
        } else {
            Console.WriteLine("The list is not empty.");
        }

        // Alternatively, using LINQ:
        if (!myList.Any()) {
            Console.WriteLine("The list is empty.");
        } else {
            Console.WriteLine("The list is not empty.");
        }
    }
}
```

